@startuml layout-pass
title Terminal — one layout pass: hbox({ "one" | border, "two" | border | flex, "three" | border | flex })

skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox

participant "Application" as A
participant "Quadtree" as QT
participant "hbox\n(Box)" as H
participant "border(one)\ngrow = 0" as B1
participant "border(two)\ngrow = 1" as B2
participant "border(three)\ngrow = 1" as B3

== trigger ==

note over A
  relayout() runs on construction, on SIGWINCH,
  and after any change to a natural size
  (label.text = ...). **Not** per frame, and
  **not** per event.
end note

A -> A : [rows, cols] = Terminal::getSize()

group measure — bottom-up, pure, no side effects
  A -> H : measure()
  H -> B1 : measure()
  B1 --> H : {5, 3}
  note right of B1
    "one" is 3 cells; border adds
    a cell on each side. A bordered
    node reports padding = 1, because
    Border::draw paints **outside**
    the child's rect.
  end note
  H -> B2 : measure()
  B2 --> H : {5, 3}
  H -> B3 : measure()
  B3 --> H : {7, 3}
  H --> A : {17, 3}\n(sum + gap*(n-1))
end

group arrange — top-down, the only thing allowed to move a widget
  A -> H : arrange({0, 0, 20, 3})
  H -> H : avail = 20 - 2*padding - gap*(n-1)

  H -> H : **1. base sizes**\n[5, 5, 7]  used = 17  totalGrow = 2
  H -> H : **2. distribute slack**\nslack = 20 - 17 = 3\n[5, 5+1.5, 7+1.5]
  H -> H : **3. snap to whole cells**\n[5, 7, 8]  — remainder carried

  note right of H
    A terminal has no fractional cells.
    Snap **once per container**, carrying
    the accumulated remainder forward, or
    1fr/1fr/1fr over 20 columns rounds to
    6+6+6 and leaves a hole.
  end note

  H -> B1 : arrange({0, 0, 5, 3})
  H -> B2 : arrange({5, 0, 7, 3})
  H -> B3 : arrange({12, 0, 8, 3})
  note right of B3
    Cross axis: Stretch gives the
    container's cross size minus padding;
    otherwise the measured size, offset
    by Start / Center / End.

    A child that is itself a Box recurses
    here — one pass, any depth.
  end note
end

group reindex — rects just moved
  A -> QT : clear()
  A -> QT : insert(each focusable leaf)
  note right of QT
    The quadtree's contract is that an object
    must be removed **before** it moves. A full
    rebuild after arrange() is the honest way
    to satisfy it, and it is cheap at terminal
    sizes. Holds Renderable* — stable, because
    the tree is retained, not rebuilt per frame.
  end note
end

group render — top-down, reads the rect, never writes it
  A -> H : render(term)
  H -> B1 : render(term)
  H -> B2 : render(term)
  H -> B3 : render(term)
  A -> A : dirty.clear()
end

note over A, B3
  Routing is unchanged and stays flat: rects are
  absolute, so a click hit-tests against the tree
  directly. Containers are layout nodes only —
  they forward no events and own no index.
end note

@enduml
